cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it as below, and please state that the
  main theorem is an implication from the printed imports A1-A8 of its section 2.4,
  with one theorem of Glimm, Jaffe and Spencer imported (Theorem 1.1.7, also used
  across strips transverse to the time-zero line, a case its printed proof does not
  reach: item A8(iv)-T), and that the human page readings of audit item C5 are open.
  Until the repair announced in the README's notice of 11 November 2026 is audited,
  please state as well that an audit of 9 November 2026 found four standard free-field
  facts used in the record without being stated or imported.
title: >-
  Removal of the spatial cutoff for weakly coupled P(phi)_2: norm convergence of
  the ground-state net on the quasi-local algebra (Part I)
abstract: >-
  Let H(g) be the spatially cutoff P(phi)_2 Hamiltonian, Omega_g its ground state,
  and omega_g the induced state on the time-zero quasi-local algebra. From one printed
  theorem of Glimm, Jaffe and Spencer (Ann. of Math. 100 (1974)), the clustering
  Theorem 1.1.7, used also across strips transverse to the time-zero line (a case its
  printed statement covers and its printed proof does not reach), together with standard
  construction inputs, the full net (omega_g) converges in norm on every local algebra in
  the weak-coupling region, with a super-polynomial rate, explicit up to one finite
  stability constant; the uniform local moment is derived in the record (Appendix D) by
  comparing a cutoff with its restriction to a box of the source's lattice squares. The
  limit is locally normal,
  translation and Z_2 invariant, and a ground state of the Glimm-Jaffe dynamics in
  the spectral sense. The proof is Hamiltonian, via a local-perturbations-perturb-
  locally estimate built on an exact spectral filter and the exact light cone. The
  repository also contains the working drafts and the adversarial audit trail.
